-- Path family + NonEmptyStr — the discriminated-union view of filesystem paths
-- and the refined-string atom they depend on.
--
-- NonEmptyStr is the first migration touching the predicate-refinement
-- codepath (Phase 1 syntax `T | <predicate>`). Its body lowers to
-- `$where: {call: ["gt", {var: "value.length"}, 0]}` — the canonical
-- call-form the parser emits, matching the storage-layer migration
-- 0040_operator_form_to_call.sql.
--
-- The Path family models filesystem paths algebraically (sister to the
-- string-side `format:path:*` named-set family). Modeled as a
-- discriminated union so "absolute vs relative" is a type-level fact:
-- you can't accidentally call `parent` on an absolute path expecting
-- a relative result. Roots are themselves a sum (PosixRoot, DriveRoot,
-- UncRoot); each segment is NameSeg / ParentSeg / CurrentSeg.
--
-- PathRoot.DriveRoot references DriveLetter — an un-migrated atom that
-- stays in `type-foundation.ts` as a TS-only inline literal until the
-- Phase 2.10 `/regex/` lexer extension lands. The `{$named: "DriveLetter"}`
-- ref resolves through the entity registry at lookup time, the same way
-- `{$named: "Bool"}` did before Bool's migration completed in Phase 2.
--
-- Note on layout: multi-line constructor decls with `|`-alternation
-- across lines need the `=` at the end of the first line and the body
-- indented under it. The brief's example with a bare opener line
-- (`PathSegment\n  = NameSeg …`) fails to parse — the parser expects
-- the right-hand side to anchor on the `=` token's column, not the
-- following line.

NonEmptyStr = String | value.length > 0

PathSegment =
  NameSeg value: NonEmptyStr
  | ParentSeg
  | CurrentSeg

PathRoot =
  PosixRoot
  | DriveRoot letter: DriveLetter
  | UncRoot server: NonEmptyStr share: NonEmptyStr

Path =
  AbsolutePath root: PathRoot segments: List PathSegment
  | RelativePath segments: List PathSegment

-- Refined-string atoms — String constrained by a named set or regex.
--
-- Deferred from Phase 2.9 pending the parseSetForm source-slice fix in
-- Phase 2.10. Each is a thin refinement: a named-set lookup (str:emoji,
-- format:path) or a regex literal that lowers to a $pattern SetExpr via
-- regexStringToPattern.
--
-- format:path:* sub-variants (posix, windows, portable, …) stay outside
-- the .fenel registry — they're presets exposed through the catalog,
-- not first-class entity atoms. Same goes for str:emoji:* sub-groups.

EmojiString = String | value ∈ str:emoji

DriveLetter = String | value ∈ /^[A-Za-z]$/

PathStr = String | value ∈ format:path
